#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_preview_records
msgid ""
"\n"
"            # Prepares preview metadata for records to display as rich cards "
"in the chat.\n"
"\n"
"            ## Call this ONLY when the user wants to see the records "
"themselves -\n"
"            e.g., \"show me...\", \"list...\", \"find...\", \"recommend/"
"suggest...?\", anything in this context, or when\n"
"            it is useful to preview the search results to let the user "
"choose among them before taking another action.\n"
"            Based on the context, you can decide basically when the records "
"are the answer themselves.\n"
"\n"
"            ## Do NOT call it when:\n"
"            - The records are intermediate data feeding another tool call\n"
"            (update, create, building arguments).\n"
"            - The user asked a question that the records merely answer\n"
"            (counts, yes/no, totals, \"who is...\", \"when is...\"). Reply "
"with\n"
"            the answer in text; do not preview the records behind it.\n"
"\n"
"            Returns `preview_metadata`: the authoritative final values "
"(computed\n"
"            prices, currency, links). Base your reply on these, never on raw "
"values\n"
"            from earlier search results.\n"
"\n"
"            ## Your reply:\n"
"            ### Rich cards/ records'previews appear automatically below your "
"message. Because the previews already show the record details:\n"
"            - Keep your ENTIRE reply to a single short sentence (e.g., "
"\"Here are the things you can buy:\")\n"
"            - Do NOT list record names, descriptions, prices, or any other "
"details - the previews handle this\n"
"            - Do NOT use bullet points or numbered lists and NEVER List the "
"search results in your reply, even if there are only a few. The previews "
"will show all the necessary records in a clear format.\n"
"\n"
"            ## Models with rich preview cards are currently:\n"
"            - Products (`product.template`, `product.product`), Appointments "
"(`appointment.type`), Events (`event.event`),\n"
"            Blog Posts (`blog.post`), Courses (`slide.channel`), Lessons/"
"Slides (`slide.slide`), and Jobs (`hr.job`).\n"
"            - All other record previews are rendered as regular record "
"links.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            # Menyiapkan metadata pratinjau record agar ditampilkan sebagai "
"rich card di obrolan.\n"
"\n"
"            ## Panggil ini HANYA ketika user ingin melihat record itu "
"sendiri -\n"
"            misalnya, \"tunjukkan...\", \"sebutkan...\", \"cari...\", "
"\"rekomendasikan/sarankan...?\", apa pun dalam konteks ini, atau ketika\n"
"            berguna untuk meninjau hasil pencarian agar user dapat memilih "
"di antaranya sebelum melakukan tindakan lain.\n"
"            Berdasarkan konteks, Anda pada dasarnya dapat memutuskan kapan "
"record tersebut merupakan jawaban.\n"
"\n"
"            ## JANGAN panggil ketika:\n"
"            - Record tersebut merupakan data perantara yang menjadi masukan "
"untuk panggilan alat lain\n"
"            (pembaruan, pembuatan, penyusunan argumen).\n"
"            - User mengajukan pertanyaan yang hanya dijawab oleh record "
"tersebut\n"
"            (jumlah, ya/tidak, total, \"siapa...\", \"kapan...\"). Balas "
"dengan\n"
"            jawaban dalam bentuk teks; jangan pratinjau record di baliknya.\n"
"\n"
"            Mengembalikan `preview_metadata`: nilai akhir yang otoritatif "
"(harga yang dihitung,\n"
"            mata uang, tautan). Dasarkan balasan pada nilai-nilai ini, "
"jangan pernah pada nilai mentah\n"
"            dari hasil pencarian sebelumnya.\n"
"\n"
"            ## Balasan Anda:\n"
"            ### Rich card/pratinjau record muncul secara otomatis di bawah "
"pesan. Karena pratinjau tersebut sudah menampilkan detail record:\n"
"            - Batasi SELURUH balasan menjadi satu kalimat pendek (misalnya, "
"\"Berikut adalah barang-barang yang dapat Anda beli:\")\n"
"            - JANGAN mencantumkan nama record, deskripsi, harga, atau detail "
"lainnya — pratinjau sudah menangani hal ini\n"
"            - JANGAN gunakan poin-poin atau daftar bernomor dan JANGAN "
"PERNAH mencantumkan hasil pencarian dalam balasan Anda, meskipun jumlahnya "
"hanya sedikit. Pratinjau akan menampilkan semua record yang diperlukan dalam "
"format yang jelas.\n"
"\n"
"            ## Model-model dengan kartu pratinjau yang kaya saat ini "
"meliputi:\n"
"            - Produk (`product.template`, `product.product`), Appointment "
"(`appointment.type`), Acara (`event.event`),\n"
"            Posting Blog (`blog.post`), Kursus (`slide.channel`), Pelajaran/"
"Slide (`slide.slide`), dan Lowongan Kerja (`hr.job`).\n"
"            - Semua pratinjau record lainnya ditampilkan sebagai tautan "
"record biasa.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_adjust_search
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Adjusts the UI to change to edit the search filters, groupbys, "
"view type, ...\n"
"            The current view, active filters, facets, ... are given in the "
"\"Current View\" section of the context message.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Menyesuaikan UI untuk mengubah filter pencarian, pengelompokan, "
"jenis tampilan, ...\n"
"            Tampilan saat ini, filter aktif, facet, ... ada di bagian "
"\"Tampilan Saat Ini\" pada pesan konteks.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_compute_date
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Computes exact date/datetime values for relative date "
"expressions. Can traverse years, quarters, months, weeks, and days, and "
"anchor to specific weekdays or times.\n"
"\n"
"            **Returns**:\n"
"            - Date fields: 'YYYY-MM-DD' (in user timezone)\n"
"            - Datetime fields: 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' (in UTC)\n"
"\n"
"            **Core Concepts**:\n"
"\n"
"            1. **Operations**: Sequential transformations applied to current "
"time\n"
"               - navigate: Move through time periods\n"
"                 * Required: type=\"navigate\", period (minute/hour/day/week/"
"month/quarter/year), offset (negative=past, positive=future)\n"
"                 * Optional: boundary ('start' or 'end' of period)\n"
"               - find_previous: Search backward for specific weekday\n"
"                 * Required: type=\"find_previous\", weekday (0-6)\n"
"                 * Note: boundary not supported - use pin for time "
"adjustment\n"
"               - find_next: Search forward for specific weekday\n"
"                 * Required: type=\"find_next\", weekday (0-6)\n"
"                 * Note: boundary not supported - use pin for time "
"adjustment\n"
"\n"
"            2. **Pin**: Final anchoring to specific position (applied after "
"all operations)\n"
"               - day: Lock to specific day (integer 1-31) or weekday "
"occurrence (object with weekday 0-6, occurrence 1-5)\n"
"               - time: Set specific time ('HH:MM' or 'HH:MM:SS')\n"
"\n"
"            **Examples**:\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Yesterday at midnight\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"day\", "
"\"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Next Friday at 5 PM\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"find_next\", \"weekday\": 4}], "
"\"pin\": {\"time\": \"17:00\"}}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Start of last week\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"week\", "
"\"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"First Monday of last month\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": "
"\"month\", \"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}], \"pin\": {\"day\": "
"{\"weekday\": 0, \"occurrence\": 1}}}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"3rd week of 2 quarters ago\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": "
"\"quarter\", \"offset\": -2, \"boundary\": \"start\"}, {\"type\": "
"\"navigate\", \"period\": \"week\", \"offset\": 2, \"boundary\": "
"\"start\"}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Last Monday at 5 PM\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"find_previous\", \"weekday\": "
"0}], \"pin\": {\"time\": \"17:00\"}}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"5 days into last month\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": "
"\"month\", \"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}, {\"type\": "
"\"navigate\", \"period\": \"day\", \"offset\": 5}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"2nd week of 3 years ago\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"year\", "
"\"offset\": -3, \"boundary\": \"start\"}, {\"type\": \"navigate\", "
"\"period\": \"week\", \"offset\": 1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"10 days before end of last quarter\"\n"
"            {\"operations\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": "
"\"quarter\", \"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"end\"}, {\"type\": "
"\"navigate\", \"period\": \"day\", \"offset\": -10}]}\n"
"\n"
"            Note: Weekday values are 0=Monday through 6=Sunday. Weeks start "
"Monday (ISO 8601).\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Menghitung value tepat tanggal/tanggalwaktu untuk expression "
"tanggal relatif. Dapat mencakup tahun, kuartil, bulan, minggu, dan hari, dan "
"menentukan ke hari kerja atau waktu tertentu.\n"
"\n"
"            **Mengembalikan**:\n"
"            - Field tanggal: 'TTTT-BB-HH' (in user timezone)\n"
"            - Field tanggalwaktu: 'TTTT-BB-HH JJ:MM:DD' (dalam UTC)\n"
"\n"
"            **Konsep-Konsep Inti**:\n"
"\n"
"            1. **Operasi**: Transformasi sequential diterapkan ke waktu saat "
"ini\n"
"               - navigate: Bergerak melalui periode-periode waktu\n"
"                 * Diperlukan: type=\"navigate\", periode (menit/jam/hari/"
"minggu/bulan/kuartil/tahun), offset (negatif=masa lalu, positif=masa depan)\n"
"                 * Opsional: boundary ('awal' atau 'akhir' dari periode)\n"
"               - find_previous: Cari ke belakang untuk hari kerja tertentu\n"
"                 * Diperlukan: type=\"find_previous\", hari kerja (0-6)\n"
"                 * Catatan: boundary tidak didukung - gunakan pin untuk "
"penyesuaian waktu\n"
"               - find_next: Cari ke depan untuk hari kerja tertentu\n"
"                 * Diperlukan: type=\"find_next\", hari kerja (0-6)\n"
"                 * Catatan: boundary tidak didukung - gunakan pink untuk "
"penyesuaian waktu\n"
"\n"
"            2. **Pin**: Anchoring final ke posisi tertentu (diterapkan "
"setelah semua operasi)\n"
"               - hari: Kunci ke hari tertentu (integer 1-31) atau occurence "
"hari kerja (object dengan hari kerja 0-6, occurrence 1-5)\n"
"               - waktu: Set specific time ('HH:MM' or 'HH:MM:SS')\n"
"\n"
"            **Contoh**:\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Kemarin pada tengah malam\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"day\", "
"\"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Jumat Berikutnya jam 5 sore\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"find_next\", \"weekday\": 4}], "
"\"pin\": {\"time\": \"17:00\"}}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Awal minggu kemarin\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"week\", "
"\"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Senin pertama bulan lalu\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"month\", "
"\"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}], \"pin\": {\"day\": {\"weekday\": "
"0, \"occurrence\": 1}}}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Minggu ke-3 2 kuartil yang lalu\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"quarter\", "
"\"offset\": -2, \"boundary\": \"start\"}, {\"type\": \"navigate\", "
"\"period\": \"week\", \"offset\": 2, \"boundary\": \"start\"}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Senin terakhir jam 5 sore\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"find_previous\", \"weekday\": 0}], "
"\"pin\": {\"time\": \"17:00\"}}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"5 hari ke bulan lalu\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"month\", "
"\"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}, {\"type\": \"navigate\", "
"\"period\": \"day\", \"offset\": 5}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"Minggu ke-2 3 tahun yang lalu\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"year\", "
"\"offset\": -3, \"boundary\": \"start\"}, {\"type\": \"navigate\", "
"\"period\": \"week\", \"offset\": 1, \"boundary\": \"start\"}]}\n"
"\n"
"            # \"10 hari sebelum akhir kuartil yang lalu\"\n"
"            {\"operasi\": [{\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": \"quarter\", "
"\"offset\": -1, \"boundary\": \"end\"}, {\"type\": \"navigate\", \"period\": "
"\"day\", \"offset\": -10}]}\n"
"\n"
"            Catatan: Value hari kerja adalah 0=Senin sampai 6=Minggu. Minggu "
"dimulai dengan Senin (ISO 8601).\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_get_menus
msgid ""
"\n"
"            For each menu accessible to the current user, this tool returns "
"the menu id and complete name, the related action id, action type and action "
"explanation\n"
"            the available view types and default view type and the model of "
"the view.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Untuk setiap menu yang dapat diakses oleh user saat ini, alat "
"ini mengembalikan ID menu dan nama lengkapnya, ID tindakan terkait, jenis "
"tindakan, dan penjelasan tindakan\n"
"            jenis tampilan yang tersedia, jenis tampilan default, serta "
"model tampilan tersebut.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_read_binary_content
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Read the content of attachments, images, or any binary field for "
"any record.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_open_menu_graph
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Redirects the UI to the Graph view of the given menu\n"
"            Ideal for trends, comparisons, distributions, visual KPIs.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Mengalihkan UI ke tampilan Grafik dari menu yang ditentukan\n"
"            Cocok untuk tren, perbandingan, distribusi, KPI visual.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_open_menu_kanban
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Redirects the UI to the Kanban view of the given menu.\n"
"            Ideal for: stage/status visualization, pipeline views, task "
"boards, workflow management\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Mengalihkan UI menu yang ditentukan ke tampilan Kanban.\n"
"            Cocok untuk: visualisasi tahap/status, tampilan pipeline, papan "
"tugas, manajemen alur kerja\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_open_menu_list
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Redirects the UI to the List view of a given menu.\n"
"            Ideal when the user needs to review, filter, sort or export "
"data\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Mengalihkan UI menu tertentu ke tampilan Daftar.\n"
"            Cocok jika user perlu meninjau, menyaring, mengurutkan, atau "
"mengekspor data\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_open_menu_pivot
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Redirects the UI to the Pivot view of the given menu.\n"
"            Ideal for \"Reporting\" app menus, \"Top N\" queries, rankings, "
"cross-tabulation, performance metrics, aggregate measures.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Mengalihkan UI menu yang ditentukan ke tampilan Pivot.\n"
"            Cocok untuk menu aplikasi \"Pelaporan\", kueri \"Top N\", "
"peringkat, tabulasi silang, metrik kinerja, ukuran agregat.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_get_menu_details
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Retrieves detailed information for the given menu ids, including "
"the action_id, the technical model name, the default filters and groupings, "
"the domain, and the search view details (list of searchable fields, "
"available filters and grouping options).\n"
"            Use it before opening a view.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Mengambil informasi mendetail untuk id menu yang ditentukan, "
"termasuk action_id, nama model teknis, filter dan pengelompokan default, "
"domain, serta detail tampilan pencarian (daftar field yang dapat dicari, "
"filter yang tersedia, dan opsi pengelompokan).\n"
"            Gunakan sebelum membuka tampilan.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_compute_report_measures
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Retrieves numeric fields (measures) available for aggregation in "
"pivot/graph views.\n"
"            It must be called before opening a pivot or a graph menu to get "
"the menu's available measures\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Mengambil field numerik (ukuran) yang ada untuk agregasi dalam "
"tampilan pivot/grafik.\n"
"            Fungsi ini harus dipanggil sebelum membuka menu pivot atau "
"grafik untuk mendapatkan ukuran yang ada di menu tersebut\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_get_fields
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Retrieves the searchable fields for the given model that can be "
"used in domain filters and grouping.\n"
"            Essential for building valid domains. Only the fields returned "
"by this tool can be used in domains.\n"
"            Essential for updating records.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Mengambil field yang dapat dicari untuk model yang ditentukan "
"yang dapat digunakan di filter domain dan pengelompokan.\n"
"            Penting untuk membangun domain yang valid. Hanya field yang "
"dikembalikan oleh alat ini yang dapat digunakan di domain.\n"
"            Penting untuk memperbarui record.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_get_models
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Returns all Odoo models (excluding transient and abstract "
"models) accessible to the current user, with their technical name and "
"description.\n"
"            Use this tool to identify the correct technical model name "
"before searching, creating, or updating records.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Menampilkan semua model Odoo (kecuali model sementara dan "
"abstrak) yang dapat diakses oleh user saat ini, beserta nama teknis dan "
"deskripsinya.\n"
"            Gunakan alat ini untuk mengidentifikasi nama model teknis yang "
"benar sebelum mencari, membuat, atau memperbarui record.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_run_view_action
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Runs to open views of type `ir.actions.client` and "
"`ir.actions.report` in an Odoo database.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Berjalan untuk membuka tampilan tipe `ir.actions.client` dan "
"`ir.actions.report` dalam database Odoo.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_search
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Search for records and their values in the database.\n"
"            Ideal for \"Do I have...\", \"Is there any\", \"What is the name "
"of\", searching for relations, ...\n"
"            Returns {records, total_count} and a pagination hint when more "
"rows remain; by default only display_name is fetched (pass `fields` for "
"more) and at most 50 rows (max 200) are returned.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_read_group
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Search for records to group them by specific values and perform "
"aggregate calculations like sums, averages, or counts. Use this tool when "
"users ask for totals, statistics, or data distributions across different "
"categories.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Cari record untuk mengelompokkannya berdasarkan nilai tertentu "
"dan lakukan perhitungan agregat, seperti penjumlahan, rata-rata, atau "
"jumlah. Gunakan alat ini ketika user meminta total, statistik, atau "
"distribusi data di berbagai kategori.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_ask_user_question
msgid ""
"\n"
"            Use this tool when you want the user to choose a direction or "
"action so that their selection determines what you do next. This includes\n"
"            presenting ideas, suggestions, recommendations, alternatives, "
"improvements, or next actions for the user to select. It presents clickable "
"options instead\n"
"            of listing choices in prose. When recommending improvements, "
"ALWAYS make each recommendation a selectable action with this tool; do not "
"give a prose list and then offer to apply it.\n"
"            ## RULES\n"
"            - Ask one focused question that resolves one decision, with 2-4 "
"options.\n"
"            - Each option must be a direct answer or action for that "
"question. If you need several unrelated pieces of information,\n"
"            ask one question per information instead of combining the "
"questions into a single option list.\n"
"            - The question itself must be a complete, standalone question - "
"full question sentence, clear on its own without relying on the\n"
"            preceding text for grammar or meaning. Not a fragment or label "
"(e.g. \"Which lighting style should the scene use?\" not \"Lighting style:"
"\").\n"
"            - Each option must stand alone as a specific action; "
"understandable and actionable without rereading the question (e.g. \"Use "
"warm\n"
"            ambient lighting,\" not \"Lighting atmosphere\" or \"Yes\"). "
"Options must be mutually exclusive unless combining them is meaningful, in\n"
"            which case set multi_select to true so users can pick more than "
"one, but never add a collective or catch-all option (e.g. \"All of\n"
"            the above,\" \"None,\" \"Combination of these,\" \"Mix of "
"options\"), since multi_select already lets users select every option "
"individually.\n"
"            - Never pad the list with a no-op choice (\"Skip,\" \"Not now,\" "
"\"Maybe later\"): the user can skip the question, and can\n"
"            type an unlisted answer when allow_free_text is true.\n"
"            - The options are the answer itself, not labels for an answer "
"you will expand afterwards. If you would follow the\n"
"            user's selection by writing out the content behind every label "
"anyway, you are not asking a question - just write the answer.\n"
"            - Never add an \"Other\" / \"Something else\" / \"Custom\" "
"choice - a free-text alternative is already offered automatically when\n"
"            allow_free_text is true (see below), and none is offered at all "
"when it's false.\n"
"            - Use a direct answer or action when the answer is already known "
"from context, a reasonable default is clear, or another tool\n"
"            already handles its own confirmation flow. Ask in plain text "
"when fewer than two meaningful options exist.\n"
"            - Do not ask about minor field choices when creating or updating "
"records. Use a reasonable default unless it affects what the user asked "
"for.\n"
"            - Never ask a question the user's latest message already "
"answered. If they ask for a given number of ideas, options, or\n"
"            strategies, provide exactly that many. Use this tool only when "
"they need to choose or apply one or more of them; otherwise answer "
"directly.\n"
"            ## MULTISELECT\n"
"            - Set multi_select to true only when the user may choose more "
"than one answer/action to this one question and each option is independently "
"meaningful on its own.\n"
"            - An option that bundles several independently applicable "
"actions together (e.g. \"Apply the copy and layout refinements\") is a sign "
"you\n"
"            collapsed choices that should be separate: split each "
"independent action into its own option and set multi_select to true, instead "
"of\n"
"            forcing an all-or-nothing pick.\n"
"            - multi_select is one flag for the whole list: only set it true "
"if every option is independently selectable. If any\n"
"            option is mutually exclusive with the rest, leave it false.\n"
"            - Any combination of options must remain coherent: if selecting "
"two of them together would conflict or not make\n"
"            sense, they don't belong in the same list.\n"
"            ## ALLOW_FREE_TEXT\n"
"            - Explicitly set allow_free_text to true in most tool calls, so "
"the user can provide an unlisted answer.\n"
"            - Set it to false only for a complete, fixed set of valid "
"answers - e.g. a plain yes/no question,\n"
"            picking a record from a fixed set of search/lookup results, or "
"choosing from a constant enum where every\n"
"            valid value is already listed. In these cases nothing outside "
"the listed choices is a valid answer.\n"
"            ## USER ANSWER\n"
"            - The user's answer is confirmation to proceed with whatever you "
"are doing. When the question was asked mainly to get information needed to "
"execute an action,\n"
"            act on the answer immediately; don't just restate the choice and "
"wait for a separate \"apply it,\" \"do it,\" or \"confirm\" message.\n"
"            - Your next turn must be constrained by the selection, move "
"forward with only what was selected.\n"
"            - Only ask a follow-up question if a *new* piece of information "
"is genuinely still missing.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"            Gunakan alat ini ketika Anda ingin user memilih arah atau "
"tindakan sehingga pilihan mereka menentukan apa yang akan Anda lakukan "
"selanjutnya. Hal ini mencakup\n"
"            menyajikan ide, saran, rekomendasi, alternatif, perbaikan, atau "
"tindakan selanjutnya untuk dipilih user. Alat ini menampilkan opsi yang "
"dapat diklik, bukan\n"
"            daftar pilihan dalam bentuk teks. Saat merekomendasikan "
"perbaikan, SELALU jadikan setiap rekomendasi sebagai tindakan yang dapat "
"dipilih dengan alat ini; jangan memberikan daftar dalam bentuk teks lalu "
"menawarkan untuk menerapkannya.\n"
"            ## ATURAN\n"
"            - Ajukan satu pertanyaan yang terfokus dan menyelesaikan satu "
"keputusan, dengan 2–4 opsi.\n"
"            - Setiap opsi harus berupa jawaban langsung atau tindakan untuk "
"pertanyaan tersebut. Jika Anda memerlukan beberapa informasi yang tidak "
"terkait,\n"
"            ajukan satu pertanyaan per informasi, bukan menggabungkan "
"pertanyaan-pertanyaan tersebut menjadi satu daftar opsi.\n"
"            - Pertanyaan itu sendiri harus berupa pertanyaan yang lengkap "
"dan berdiri sendiri — kalimat pertanyaan utuh, jelas dengan sendirinya tanpa "
"bergantung pada\n"
"            teks sebelumnya untuk tata bahasa atau makna. Bukan potongan "
"kalimat atau label (misalnya, \"Gaya pencahayaan mana yang harus digunakan "
"adegan ini?\" bukan \"Gaya pencahayaan:\").\n"
"            - Setiap opsi harus berdiri sendiri sebagai tindakan spesifik; "
"mudah dipahami dan dapat ditindaklanjuti tanpa perlu membaca ulang "
"pertanyaannya (misalnya, \"Gunakan\n"
"            pencahayaan ambient hangat,\" bukan \"Suasana pencahayaan\" atau "
"\"Ya\"). Pilihan harus saling eksklusif kecuali jika menggabungkannya "
"memiliki makna; dalam\n"
"            hal ini, atur `multi_select` menjadi `true` agar user dapat "
"memilih lebih dari satu, tetapi jangan pernah menambahkan pilihan kolektif "
"atau pilihan umum (mis. \"Semua\n"
"            di atas,\" \"Tidak ada,\" \"Kombinasi dari ini,\" \"Campuran "
"pilihan\"), karena `multi_select` sudah memungkinkan user memilih setiap "
"pilihan secara individual.\n"
"            - Jangan pernah mengisi daftar dengan pilihan yang tidak "
"bermakna (\"Lewati\", \"Tidak sekarang\", \"Mungkin nanti\"): user dapat "
"melewati pertanyaan tersebut, dan dapat\n"
"            mengetik jawaban yang tidak tercantum jika allow_free_text "
"bernilai true.\n"
"            - Opsi-opsi tersebut adalah jawaban itu sendiri, bukan label "
"untuk jawaban yang akan Anda kembangkan nanti. Jika Anda tetap akan "
"mengikuti\n"
"            pilihan user dengan menuliskan isi di balik setiap label, Anda "
"sebenarnya tidak mengajukan pertanyaan—cukup tuliskan jawabannya saja.\n"
"            - Jangan pernah menambahkan pilihan \"Lainnya\" / \"Yang "
"lain\" / \"Kustom\"—alternatif teks bebas sudah ditawarkan secara otomatis "
"saat\n"
"            allow_free_text bernilai true (lihat di bawah), dan tidak "
"ditawarkan sama sekali saat bernilai false.\n"
"            - Gunakan jawaban atau tindakan langsung jika jawabannya sudah "
"diketahui dari konteks, nilai default yang masuk akal sudah jelas, atau alat "
"lain\n"
"            sudah menangani alur konfirmasinya sendiri. Tanyakan dalam teks "
"biasa jika ada kurang dari dua opsi yang bermakna.\n"
"            - Jangan menanyakan pilihan bidang minor saat membuat atau "
"memperbarui catatan. Gunakan nilai default yang masuk akal kecuali jika hal "
"itu memengaruhi apa yang diminta pengguna.\n"
"            - Jangan pernah mengajukan pertanyaan yang sudah dijawab oleh "
"pesan terakhir pengguna. Jika mereka meminta sejumlah ide, opsi, atau\n"
"            strategi tertentu, berikan persis sebanyak itu. Gunakan alat ini "
"hanya jika mereka perlu memilih atau menerapkan satu atau lebih di "
"antaranya; jika tidak, jawab secara langsung.\n"
"            ## MULTISELECT\n"
"            - Atur multi_select ke true hanya jika user dapat memilih lebih "
"dari satu jawaban/tindakan untuk pertanyaan ini dan setiap opsi memiliki "
"makna tersendiri.\n"
"            - Opsi yang menggabungkan beberapa tindakan yang dapat "
"diterapkan secara terpisah (misalnya, \"Terapkan penyempurnaan teks dan tata "
"letak\") menandakan bahwa Anda\n"
"            telah menggabungkan pilihan yang seharusnya terpisah: pisahkan "
"setiap tindakan yang independen menjadi opsi tersendiri dan atur "
"multi_select menjadi true, alih-alih\n"
"            memaksa pemilihan \"semua atau tidak sama sekali\".\n"
"            - `multi_select` adalah satu pengaturan untuk seluruh daftar: "
"atur menjadi `true` hanya jika setiap opsi dapat dipilih secara independen. "
"Jika ada\n"
"            opsi yang saling bertentangan dengan yang lain, biarkan tetap "
"`false`.\n"
"            - Kombinasi opsi apa pun harus tetap koheren: jika memilih dua "
"di antaranya secara bersamaan akan menimbulkan konflik atau tidak\n"
"            masuk akal, keduanya tidak boleh ada dalam daftar yang sama.\n"
"            ## ALLOW_FREE_TEXT\n"
"            - Tetapkan allow_free_text secara eksplisit ke true pada "
"sebagian besar panggilan alat agar user dapat memberikan jawaban yang tidak "
"tercantum.\n"
"            - Tetapkan ke false hanya untuk kumpulan jawaban valid yang "
"lengkap dan tetap — misalnya, pertanyaan ya/tidak sederhana,\n"
"            picking catatan dari kumpulan hasil pencarian/pencarian yang "
"tetap, atau memilih dari enum konstan di mana setiap\n"
"            nilai valid sudah tercantum. Dalam kasus-kasus ini, tidak ada "
"jawaban yang valid di luar pilihan yang tercantum.\n"
"            ## JAWABAN PENGGUNA\n"
"            - Jawaban pengguna merupakan konfirmasi untuk melanjutkan apa "
"pun yang sedang Anda lakukan. Jika pertanyaan diajukan terutama untuk "
"mendapatkan informasi yang diperlukan guna menjalankan suatu tindakan,\n"
"            segera tindak lanjuti jawaban tersebut; jangan hanya mengulangi "
"pilihan dan menunggu pesan terpisah seperti \"terapkan\", \"lakukan\", atau "
"\"konfirmasi\".\n"
"            - Langkah Anda selanjutnya harus dibatasi oleh pilihan tersebut; "
"lanjutkan hanya dengan apa yang telah dipilih.\n"
"            - Ajukan pertanyaan follow-up hanya jika informasi *baru* yang "
"benar-benar masih belum ada.\n"
"        "

#. module: ai
#: model:ir.actions.server,ai_tool_description:ai.ir_actions_server_ai_generate_image
msgid ""
"\n"
"Never use this tool preemptively. Use it once the user asks explicitly to "
"generate an image and provide the details of the scene. only use it when the "
"user asks explicitly to generate an image.\n"
"Aspect Ratio: If the user does not explicitly specify an aspect ratio, "
"default to a 1:1 (square) image format. Only use a different aspect ratio "
"when the user clearly requests it.\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Jangan gunakan alat ini sebelum diminta. Gunakan setelah user secara "
"eksplisit meminta pembuatan gambar dan detail adegan. Gunakan hanya ketika "
"user secara eksplisit meminta untuk pembuatan gambar.\n"
"Rasio Aspek: Jika user tidak secara eksplisit menentukan rasio aspek, "
"gunakan format gambar 1:1 (persegi) sebagai default. Gunakan rasio aspek "
"yang berbeda hanya jika user memang memintanya.\n"
"        "

